From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gitStoneLabs <roger@stonelabs.dev>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 15:50:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dbus_exporter: skip executables that fail to introspect

Buildroot 2022.02 pins host-systemd to 250.4 which has a buffer-overflow
bug in its --bus-introspect argument parsing. Older glibc was permissive;
newer glibc (2.39+) catches it via fortify-source and aborts the binary
with SIGABRT before any output is produced.

Since the interfaces XML files this script generates are pure metadata
(D-Bus introspection data, only consumed by introspection tools at runtime),
losing them does not affect the target rootfs at all. Patch the script to
log the failure and continue rather than aborting the entire host-systemd
build.

Signed-off-by: gitStoneLabs <roger@stonelabs.dev>
---
 tools/dbus_exporter.py | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/dbus_exporter.py b/tools/dbus_exporter.py
index 0000001..0000002 100755
--- a/tools/dbus_exporter.py
+++ b/tools/dbus_exporter.py
@@ -36,7 +36,10 @@ def iterate_executables(output_dir, executables):
     output_dir.mkdir(mode=0o755, exist_ok=True)

     for exe in executables:
-        extract_interfaces_xml(output_dir, exe)
+        try:
+            extract_interfaces_xml(output_dir, exe)
+        except Exception as e:
+            print(f"WARNING: skipping {exe} interfaces export ({type(e).__name__}: {e}). Buildroot 2022.02 systemd 250.4 has a buffer-overflow bug in --bus-introspect that newer glibc fortify-source catches. The interfaces XML is metadata only — target rootfs is unaffected.", flush=True)


 def main():
--
2.39.2
